  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Crl.Rev.P./383/2009 on 28 January, 2019 Author: Hitesh Kumar Sarma Bench: Hitesh Kumar Sarma Page N Gahc010006102009 In The Gauhati High Court (The High Court Of Assam: Nagaland: Mizoram & Arunachal Pradesh) Criminal Revision Petition No. 383 of 2009 Sri Sanjan Dutta @ Sri Sanjay Dutta, Son of Sri Makhan Lal Dutta, Resident of Khageswar Road, P.O. and P.S. Tinsukia, Dist. Tinsukia, Assam. ----- Accused/Petitioner. - Versus - The State of Assam. ----- Respondent/Opposite Parties. Before Hon'ble Mr. Justice Hitesh Kumar Sarma Advocates for accused-petitioner : Ms. B Sarma, Advocate. Advocate for Respondent : Mr. Rj Barua, Additional Public Prosecutor, Assam. Date of hearing and Judgment & Order : 28th of January, 2019. Judgment",
    "facts": "4. The fact of the case is that, on 12-10-2006, the Food Inspector examined, as PW1, inspected the M/S Delight Bakery at Tinsukia. Suspecting the bread manufactured there to be adulterated, after observing all required formalities, the Food Inspector had taken sample of such bread. He purchased six breads, weighing 400 grams each, totalling 2400 grams at a total price of Rs. 72/-. 5. The sample, so collected, were packed in such a manner so as to prevent moisture etc., and forwarded a part of the sample for analysis by Public Analyst, Assam, a part of the sample was sent to the Joint Director and the other part founded to the Court as per procedure. 6. The Public Analysts, after necessary examination, gave his report, vide Ext. 14. Thereafter, the PW1, Food Inspector, lodged a complaint with the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Tinsukia, after obtaining necessary sanction from the competent authority, i.e., the Joint Director of Health Services. 7. On receipt of the complaint, the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Tinsukia, after exhausting all required formalities, explained the offence to the petitioner, under Section 16 read with Section 7 of the PFA Act, to which the petitioner pleaded innocence; therefore, the trial commenced. 8. In this case, prosecution examined as many as 2 witnesses, the Food Inspector/the Page No.# 3/5 complainant as well as PW2, the Office Peon of the Office of the Food Inspector, who accompanied PW1 to the M/S Delight Bakery at Tinsukia, at the relevant point of time.",
